// marking schemes bundle a series' sets in one PDF; the set's own section (its paper code in the
// page header / footer) was read. Where a bank step had carried scheme residue ("½ , ½", the next
// question's text) or was truncated, the step was re-cut from the scheme (`stepsRecut`, `scheme`
// says what was completed). A row's "[½ mark]" prefixes are normalised to "[0.5 marks]" (the form
// the board-question picker reads).

